Dawamu OS - KCSE Set Book Study Guide
TITLE: The Samaritan
AUTHOR: John Lara
GENRE: Compulsory KCSE English Literature Play

SETTING:
The fictional Maracas Municipality, plagued by systemic graft, ghost workers, crumbling infrastructure, and moral decay.

PLOT SUMMARY:
Two students at Sagrada Secondary School (Montano and Alvita), mentored by their principled teacher Nicole, design a revolutionary mobile application named "The Samaritan". The app crowdsources evidence of civic corruption, triggering panic among Mayor Mossi and the Municipal Council. When threats, bribes, and false police charges fail to derail Nicole, the corrupt cartel faces public collapse and legal arrest.

CHARACTERS:
1. Teacher Nicole: Moral backbone, advocate of social justice.
2. Mayor Mossi: Corrupt, arrogant mayor who tries to escape accountability by finger-pointing.
3. Inspector Bembe: Corrupt police head who fabricates evidence against Nicole.
4. Ramdaye, Ted, and Seymour: Council members involved in black-market deals and tender fraud.
5. Montano and Alvita: Visionary students symbolizing the triumph of technology and youth.

CORE THEMES:
- The Blight of Corruption in Public Service.
- The Transformative Role of Youth and Technology.
- Abuse of Police Power and State Institutions.
- Moral Integrity and Civic Courage.

